  "title": "P-ary m-sequence-based c-VEP dataset from Martínez-Cagigal et al. (2023)",
  "description": "EEG recordings from 16 healthy participants using a code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) brain-computer interface based on p-ary (non-binary) m-sequences. Sixteen EEG channels were sampled at 256 Hz across five conditions (stored as sessions), each with eight runs (six for training, two for testing). The dataset supports research on more comfortable c-VEP BCI stimulation and is distributed in BIDS format via MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded from 16 channels at 256 Hz (standard_1005 montage, 50 Hz line frequency). Each participant completed five conditions, stored as separate sessions, with eight runs per session (six training, two test). Visual stimuli were presented with intensity levels derived from p-ary m-sequences, giving 11 event labels.",
